Local changes to pico 4.3 for RhapsodiOS
========================================

This is pico 4.3L: pico 4.3 as released in pine 4.50, modified locally
to build on Rhapsody (Mac OS X Server 1.x) for RhapsodiOS. As the
University of Washington's legal notices (CPYRIGHT) request, the version
number carries the "L" suffix and the local changes are listed here.

Source: https://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/gnu2/pine/old/pine4.50.tar.Z
        (pine4.50/pico, pine4.50/doc/pico.1, pine4.50/CPYRIGHT)

Layout
  The contents of pine4.50/pico sit at the top of this directory,
  together with pine4.50/doc/pico.1 and pine4.50/CPYRIGHT. pico is
  built as a tool of basic_cmds through pb_makefiles.

Changed upstream files
  pico.h               version string "4.3" -> "4.3L"
  osdep/unix           #define MAX guarded with #ifndef MAX; Rhapsody's
                       <sys/param.h> already defines it.

New files: a Rhapsody port alongside the existing ones
  osdep/os-rhp.h       derived from os-nxt.h.  POSIX termios instead of
                       sgtty, MAILDIR /var/mail, no sys_errlist or
                       sys_nerr declarations (stdio.h declares them), and
                       HAVE_WAIT_UNION off so wait() gets the int it is
                       declared to take.
  osdep/os-rhp.ic      derived from os-nxt.ic.  raw.ios instead of
                       raw.brk, and libc's getcwd instead of
                       osdep/getcwd.

Line endings
  makefile.cyg, osdep/os-cyg.h, osdep/os-cyg.ic and resource.h (Cygwin
  and Windows only) are stored with LF line endings instead of CRLF, as
  the repository's .gitattributes requires.

RhapsodiOS build glue
  Makefile, Makefile.preamble, Makefile.postamble, PB.project and this
  file.  They build what makefile.nxt builds for pico, with -Drhp and
  without pilot: os.h and pico_os.c are generated from osdep/os-rhp.h
  and osdep/os-rhp.ic with osdep/includer, and the objects are linked
  directly instead of through libpico.a, since ranlib can't index an
  archive of fat objects.  termcap comes from System instead of
  -ltermcap.
